From: Raag Jadav <raag.jadav@intel.com>
Subject: [PATCH] fixup! drm/xe/pm: Introduce xe_device_suspend/resume()

Don't drop dma mappings of pinned external bos during PCIe FLR prepare.

xe_bo_pci_dev_remove_pinned() is a pci_device *removal* helper. FLR is not
removal: it resets the state of the PCI function, not the IOMMU domain the
function is attached to, so the IOVA mappings of pinned external bos stay
valid across the reset and do not need to be torn down.

Calling it from the FLR prepare path is wrong for two reasons.

First, it is unpaired. The resume side takes the flr == true branch, which
only calls xe_bo_restore_map() (kernel bos, GGTT only) and never touches
xe->pinned.late.external. There is also no helper that could be added to
pair with it: the only thing that re-creates the sg is xe_bo_restore_pinned(),
which returns early when the bo has no backup object, and FLR deliberately
skips xe_bo_evict_all() so no backup object is ever created. The bos are
therefore left permanently with ttm_bo->sg == NULL and xe_tt->sg == NULL
while still pinned, still on the list, and with the device advertised as
usable again.

Second, it performs an uninterruptible, untimed dma_fence_wait() via
xe_tile_migrate_wait() after xe_irq_suspend(). If the migrate queue has an
in-flight job when FLR is triggered, that fence is not guaranteed to have
been signalled: the TDR queued by xe_guc_submit_pause_abort() takes the
timeout_needs_gt_reset() path, which is unconditionally true for
EXEC_QUEUE_FLAG_KERNEL. drm_sched_invalidate_job(job, 2) is false on the
first pass, so it calls xe_gt_reset_async() and goes to 'rearm' without
signalling anything. xe_gt_reset_async() is itself a no-op here, because
uc_flr_prepare() already set guc->submission_state.stopped via
xe_uc_reset_prepare(). Nothing else signals the fence, so the wait never
returns.

Dropping the call removes both problems. CPU mappings are still torn down
by unmap_mapping_range(), which is what userspace needs to re-fault against
post-FLR state.

Also revert the export of xe_bo_pci_dev_remove_pinned() added for this
caller, since xe_bo_pci_dev_remove_all() is once again its only user.

Signed-off-by: Raag Jadav <raag.jadav@intel.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_bo_evict.c | 8 +-------
 drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_bo_evict.h | 1 -
 drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_device.c   | 14 +++++++++++---
 3 files changed, 12 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_bo_evict.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_bo_evict.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_bo_evict.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_bo_evict.c
@@ -299,13 +299,7 @@ int xe_bo_restore_late(struct xe_device *xe)
 	return ret;
 }
 
-/**
- * xe_bo_pci_dev_remove_pinned() - Unmap external bos
- * @xe: xe device
- *
- * Drop dma mappings of all external pinned bos.
- */
-void xe_bo_pci_dev_remove_pinned(struct xe_device *xe)
+static void xe_bo_pci_dev_remove_pinned(struct xe_device *xe)
 {
 	struct xe_tile *tile;
 	unsigned int id;
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_bo_evict.h b/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_bo_evict.h
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_bo_evict.h
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_bo_evict.h
@@ -16,7 +16,6 @@ int xe_bo_restore_early(struct xe_device *xe);
 int xe_bo_restore_late(struct xe_device *xe);
 int xe_bo_restore_map(struct xe_device *xe);
 
-void xe_bo_pci_dev_remove_pinned(struct xe_device *xe);
 void xe_bo_pci_dev_remove_all(struct xe_device *xe);
 
 int xe_bo_pinned_init(struct xe_device *xe);
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_device.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_device.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_device.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_device.c
@@ -1620,9 +1620,16 @@ int xe_device_suspend(struct xe_device *xe, bool flr)
 	xe_irq_suspend(xe);
 
 	if (flr) {
-		/* TODO: Drop all user bos */
-		xe_bo_pci_dev_remove_pinned(xe);
-
+		/*
+		 * Note that dma mappings of pinned external bos are deliberately
+		 * left in place. FLR resets the state of the PCI function, not the
+		 * IOMMU domain it is attached to, so those mappings remain valid
+		 * across the reset. There is also nothing on the resume side that
+		 * could re-establish them: xe_bo_restore_pinned() is a no-op
+		 * without a backup object, and we skip xe_bo_evict_all() above.
+		 *
+		 * TODO: Drop all user bos
+		 */
 		unmap_mapping_range(xe->drm.anon_inode->i_mapping, 0, 0, 1);
 	} else {
 		xe_display_pm_suspend_late(xe);
